    {
      "slug": "landscape-by-sesshu",
      "title": "Landscape by Sesshū",
      "year": 1507,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/Landscape_by_Sesshu_%28Ohara%29.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 1763,
      "imageHeight": 6064,
      "story": "Landscape by Sesshū is one of the most securely authenticated works of the Japanese Muromachi period artist Sesshū (1420–1506). It is an ink wash landscape (山水図) in the private collection of the Ōhara family in Kurashiki, Okayama Prefecture, Japan. The hanging scroll has been designated a National Treasure.",
      "facts": [
        "Subsequently disappearing from the record, it turned up in a \"curio dealer's shop\" in Kyoto in 1906.",
        "Sold for ten thousand yen, it was later acquired by Magosaburō Ōhara for the sum of 160,000 yen."
      ],
      "wikipediaUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landscape_by_Sessh%C5%AB",
      "sitelinks": 4,
